      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "When water freezes, it expands and may widen a crack.",
      "file": "af_bella-e5-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 3.43
    },
    {
      "id": "e6-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Follow roots and flowing water. Separate breaking rock from moving pieces.",
      "file": "af_bella-e6-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.97
    },
    {
      "id": "e6-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Growing roots can widen cracks. Flowing water can carry loose pieces to a new place.",
      "file": "af_bella-e6-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 5.38
    },
    {
      "id": "e6-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Sort these two recorded events.",
      "file": "af_bella-e6-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 1.81
    },
    {
      "id": "e6-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A small stone arrives downstream. Does that prove it broke there?",
      "file": "af_bella-e6-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 3.97
    },
    {
      "id": "e6-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e6-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e6-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Roots can widen cracks. Moving water can carry loose rock pieces.",
      "file": "af_bella-e6-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 4.42
    },
    {
      "id": "e7-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Look beneath the surface. Soil is more than tiny pieces of rock.",
      "file": "af_bella-e7-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.35
    },
    {
      "id": "e7-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Soil can contain mineral particles, decaying organic matter, water, and air.",
      "file": "af_bella-e7-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 5.38
    },
    {
      "id": "e7-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Match each soil clue to its part.",
      "file": "af_bella-e7-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 1.94
    },
    {
      "id": "e7-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Which statement connects soil and plant life?",
      "file": "af_bella-e7-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.47
    },
    {
      "id": "e7-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e7-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e7-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Soil contains mineral particles and organic matter, with water and air in its spaces.",
      "file": "af_bella-e7-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 5.59
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Prepare two tests that differ only in the soil sample.",
      "file": "af_bella-e8-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 3.29
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A fair comparison keeps the water amount, soil volume, container, and observation time the same.",
      "file": "af_bella-e8-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 6.89
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "What changes, and what stays the same?",
      "file": "af_bella-e8-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.41
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A gets 100 mL; B gets 200 mL. Is this a fair comparison?",
      "file": "af_bella-e8-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 5.4
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e8-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "To compare soil samples, I keep the water amount and test conditions the same.",
      "file": "af_bella-e8-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 4.97
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Run three example models. Read the water collected below each cup.",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "In this example, A lets more water through in one minute than B or C. The result describes these samples and conditions.",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 8.21
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Run each sample model and compare the readings.",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.9
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Which sample lets the most water through in one minute?",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.94
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "What can this experiment support?",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.88
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-step3",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-step3.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e9-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "In this test, sample A lets the most water through in one minute.",
      "file": "af_bella-e9-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 3.9
    },
    {
      "id": "e10-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Follow an earthworm tunnel. Connect animal actions with soil spaces.",
      "file": "af_bella-e10-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.61
    },
    {
      "id": "e10-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Burrowing animals can mix soil and make paths for air and water. An earthworm is not a beetle larva.",
      "file": "af_bella-e10-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 6.72
    },
    {
      "id": "e10-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Arrange a possible chain of events.",
      "file": "af_bella-e10-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.07
    },
    {
      "id": "e10-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Must an earthworm become a beetle, like a mealworm?",
      "file": "af_bella-e10-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 3.11
    },
    {
      "id": "e10-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e10-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e10-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Burrowing animals make tunnels that help air and water move through soil.",
      "file": "af_bella-e10-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 4.27
    },
    {
      "id": "e11-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Use the test record and a fictional plant brief. Choose evidence, not a favorite color.",
      "file": "af_bella-e11-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 5.55
    },
    {
      "id": "e11-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A useful choice depends on the plant and the test conditions. There is no single best soil for every plant.",
      "file": "af_bella-e11-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 7.17
    },
    {
      "id": "e11-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Our model plant needs 30–40 mL collected in this test. Which sample fits?",
      "file": "af_bella-e11-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 5.33
    },
    {
      "id": "e11-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Choose two pieces of evidence for your recommendation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e11-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 3.03
    },
    {
      "id": "e11-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e11-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e11-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "I choose sample B because 35 mL fits this model plant’s target.",
      "file": "af_bella-e11-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 4.93
    },
    {
      "id": "e12-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Review the claims for our research exhibition. Correct mistakes with evidence from the chapter.",
      "file": "af_bella-e12-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 5.53
    },
    {
      "id": "e12-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Strong explanations connect observations, fair tests, and carefully limited conclusions.",
      "file": "af_bella-e12-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 6.19
    },
    {
      "id": "e12-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Place each claim in the correct display.",
      "file": "af_bella-e12-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.39
    },
    {
      "id": "e12-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A new model plant needs 50–70 mL collected. Which sample now fits?",
      "file": "af_bella-e12-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 5.1
    },
    {
      "id": "e12-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-e12-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "e12-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "When the plant’s needs change, my choice may change. I use the test record to explain why.",
